From: <maintainer>
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: freezer: prevent spurious transition into non-frozen state

Backport of the upstream/LineageOS commit that fixed the "Chrome causes
system instability" bug (LineageOS/issues#756) on other 24.0 kernels.

Neither LineageOS/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8250 (lineage-24.0) nor
LineageOS/android_kernel_qcom_sm8250 (lineage-20) carries this fix yet:
cgroup_leave_frozen() still contains the old
`if (unlikely(current->frozen)) recalc_sigpending()` path.

When freezing races with waking a task (vfork(), do_signal_stop()), the
cgroup's nr_frozen_tasks counter and state can transition spuriously to
"unfrozen" while a task is still frozen. The task then never leaves
do_freezer_trap(), the system hangs and the hardware watchdog reboots
the device (observed on elish as `sysrq: Kill All Tasks` in the kernel
log right before reboot).

Reference commits (LineageOS/android_kernel_qcom_sm8150, lineage-20):
  7a05073b  UPSTREAM: cgroup: prevent spurious transition into non-frozen state
  28586903  UPSTREAM: cgroup: get rid of cgroup_freezer_frozen_exit()

Tested-on: lineage_elish (Xiaomi Pad 5 Pro), 4.19.325-cip136, kernel
commit 6b34d2476532.

---
 kernel/cgroup/freezer.c | 19 +++++--------------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/cgroup/freezer.c b/kernel/cgroup/freezer.c
--- a/kernel/cgroup/freezer.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/freezer.c
@@ -139,19 +139,13 @@
 		cgroup_update_frozen(cgrp);
 		WARN_ON_ONCE(!current->frozen);
 		current->frozen = false;
+	} else if (!(current->jobctl & JOBCTL_TRAP_FREEZE)) {
+		spin_lock(&current->sighand->siglock);
+		current->jobctl |= JOBCTL_TRAP_FREEZE;
+		set_thread_flag(TIF_SIGPENDING);
+		spin_unlock(&current->sighand->siglock);
 	}
 	spin_unlock_irq(&css_set_lock);
-
-	if (unlikely(current->frozen)) {
-		/*
-		 * If the task remained in the frozen state,
-		 * make sure it won't reach userspace without
-		 * entering the signal handling loop.
-		 */
-		spin_lock_irq(&current->sighand->siglock);
-		recalc_sigpending();
-		spin_unlock_irq(&current->sighand->siglock);
-	}
 }
 
